# ---------------- Python ----------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ---------------- Virtual environments ----------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
_envtest/

# ---------------- Generated data (NEVER commit data) ----------------
# The GENERATOR is committed; its OUTPUT is not.
data/*
!data/.gitkeep
!data/spec.md

# ---------------- Trained model artifacts ----------------
# A model is only reproducible if we ship the exact bytes we measured, so the
# trained artifacts DO travel with the repository. This matters because the
# models are (re)trained on Google Colab -- see docs/COLAB_RETRAIN.md -- and the
# demo machine, the Docker image and the judges must all be looking at the same
# scorecard. Committing the artifact is what guarantees that.
#
# If you retrain, the artifact changes: that is a real change worth reviewing
# and committing, not noise to be ignored.
#
# ORDER MATTERS, AND SO DOES THE COMMENT FORMAT. Two mistakes were live here and
# neither was visible from reading the file:
#
#   1. `models/*` sat AFTER the negations. In gitignore the LAST matching rule
#      wins, so it overrode every one of them and nothing in models/ was ever
#      tracked -- a fresh clone had no scorecard, and the numbers quoted
#      throughout the documentation could not be checked against it.
#   2. `!models/risk.joblib   # RandomForest risk scorer` is not a pattern with a
#      comment. A `#` only starts a comment at the beginning of a line, so the
#      whole string was the pattern, spaces and prose included, and it matched
#      nothing.
#
# Broad ignore first, then the exceptions, one pattern per line, comments above.
models/*
!models/.gitkeep
# RandomForest risk scorer (model #2)
!models/risk.joblib
# IsolationForest anomaly detector (model #1)
!models/anomaly.joblib
# the exact feature order the models expect
!models/feature_columns.json
# the measured scorecard, quoted in every report
!models/metrics.json
# versions that produced the artifacts (compatibility check)
!models/ENVIRONMENT.txt
# the training distribution the drift check compares against -- without it the
# console can only say "not measured"
!models/reference_distribution.json

# ---------------- Uploads / runtime output ----------------
uploads/
out/
*.log

# ---------------- Offline wheel cache (large, rebuildable) ----------------
# The DIRECTORY is tracked (via .gitkeep) but its contents are not. A fresh clone
# then still has a `wheels/` for the Dockerfile to COPY, so `docker build` works
# on a machine that was never connected to anything.
wheels/*
!wheels/.gitkeep

# ---------------- OS / editor ----------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp